{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>It shall blossom abundantly.</b> The land of Israel or Jerusalem." "<b>Yes, it exults and rejoices.</b> The tav [in תפרח] is like the tav [in גילת לב]; some say that [גילת] refers back to Lebanon itself." "<b>They.</b> The inhabitants of Jerusalem."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {1 "The argument turns on the tav of תפרח (35:2) being compared to the tav in the phrase גילת לב (elsewhere in Scripture); Ibn Ezra's syntax is terse and the reference to Lebanon (הר לבנון, 35:2) may involve a textual variant regarding the lemma."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:56:45.026941363Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}